course: dictionary
lesson: 6356
title: A name that became a word
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Mozart is a name, so it is a proper noun: it names one particular person, and it always starts with a capital letter. Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart was a famous composer of classical music from Austria. He lived more than two hundred years ago, and he wrote music from the age of five.
explain: Sometimes a name becomes a word people use in other ways. Informally, «a Mozart» means a child who is very talented, especially at music. The words around it are your clues: they tell you whether the word names a person or describes a quality.
explain: Read this sentence: «Mozart kept a pet starling that sang a tune from his piano music.» Here Mozart is the man himself. Now read the brain myths text, which says that playing Mozart to babies makes them cleverer. That is a myth, so when you see a claim like this, check the context and the facts before you believe it.
fact: Mozart is a proper noun, a name, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Mozart» means Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart, a famous Austrian composer of classical music.
fact: Mozart wrote music from the age of five and died young, at 35.
fact: «A Mozart» (informal) means a child who is very talented, especially at music.
fact: The «Mozart effect» is a myth: later studies found no lasting cleverness from listening to Mozart.
exercise: Which of these is a proper noun? | music | *Mozart | dog | piano
exercise: «Mozart wrote music from the age of five.» How old was Mozart when he started writing music? | Three | Ten | *Five | Thirty-five
exercise: Jayden says «a Mozart» must be a slow, sad song. What does «a Mozart» mean in informal use? | A slow, sad song | *A very talented child, especially at music | A type of starling | A kind of piano
test: «Mozart» is a name, so it begins with what? | a small letter | a number | *a capital letter | a question mark
test: Mozart died young, at what age? | 53 | 70 | *35 | 25
exam: Which is the correct way to write Mozart's name? | *Mozart | mozart | MOZART | mOZART
